-- Fold dictionaries: `(<>field)` signature constraints.
--
-- The constraint declares a hidden leading "dictionary" parameter holding the
-- merge of every in-scope `field` value. The caller passes ONLY the visible
-- arguments; at the callsite the compiler collects all in-scope `field`
-- records and merges them with `base.unify` from `{}` (innermost scope wins
-- on conflicting keys), passing the merged record as the dictionary. The body
-- reads it through `^field`.
--
-- Here `logCtx` appears in TWO scopes: nested `outer.logCtx` supplies
-- `service`, the inner `logCtx` supplies `requestId`. `mylog` collects and
-- merges both automatically.
with {
(<>logCtx) => Text -> IO {}  mylog
mylog (\msg -> base.println (base.show ^logCtx ++ " | " ++ msg))
}
(do
    (with {logCtx {service "shop"}} (mylog "single"))
    (with {outer {logCtx {service "shop"}}} (
        with {logCtx {requestId 42}} (
            mylog "merged"))))
